From: OHOS Dev <dev@ohos.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0117] Fix PATH missing /system/bin on OHOS causing FileNotFoundError

On HarmonyOS, essential commands like cat/sed/grep/sh live in /system/bin/
but this path is not in the default PATH. This causes test_restore_signals
(and any user code using subprocess with bare command names) to fail with
FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'cat'.

Fix: Add /system/bin to PATH in _harmonyos_compat.py init().

---
 Lib/_harmonyos_compat.py | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Lib/_harmonyos_compat.py b/Lib/_harmonyos_compat.py
index abcdef..1234567 100644
--- a/Lib/_harmonyos_compat.py
+++ b/Lib/_harmonyos_compat.py
@@ -66,6 +66,14 @@ def _apply_compat_layer():
     if not _is_harmonyos():
         _log("Not HarmonyOS, skipping compatibility layer")
         return
 
+    # ============================================================
+    # Ensure /system/bin is in PATH (cat/sh/sed/grep etc. live there)
+    # ============================================================
+    _path = os.environ.get('PATH', '')
+    if '/system/bin' not in _path:
+        os.environ['PATH'] = '/system/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:' + _path
+        _log(f"Added /system/bin to PATH")
+
     _log("Detected HarmonyOS, applying compatibility layer")
 
     # ============================================================

